The size of the logical volume to provision, as a size expression, or as the
`<n>%{FREE|PVS|VG}` share of the volume group lvm2 computes.

A share is handed to lvcreate as written, and lvm2 resolves it once, when the
volume is created. om never learns what it came out as, so a volume sized that
way cannot be grown by a resize, which refuses it rather than writing a size
over the share.

A share om computes is written as an arithmetic expression over the capacity
of the volume group resource, and can be grown:

	size = $(50% * {disk#vg.capacity})
